What about
eight more verses?

13:17.356 --> 13:19.190
Let's go, Pam.
We're leaving.

13:19.224 --> 13:21.526
But, Dad,
Chris treats me really well.

13:21.560 --> 13:23.828
He gave me
this diamond necklace.

13:23.862 --> 13:25.630
That's my diamond necklace!

13:25.664 --> 13:27.498
Cool it. I'm trying to get laid.

13:27.533 --> 13:29.434
Look, this ain't
happening, Pam.

13:29.468 --> 13:31.302
Straight up.
You ain't swervin' with him,

13:31.336 --> 13:33.838
you ain't gonna shump-a-jump,
you're not hollerin' at him,

13:33.872 --> 13:35.807
you ain't his shorty
or his boo.

13:35.841 --> 13:38.276
Oh, my God, Lois, I think
he just summoned Candyman.

13:38.310 --> 13:39.811
You're a fool.

13:49.332 --> 13:51.233
I was hoping
they'd be darker.

13:56.824 --> 13:59.525
God, I miss Pam
so much.

13:59.560 --> 14:01.928
I don't think
I can live without her.

14:01.962 --> 14:04.364
It's okay, Chris.
Hey, here's someone your type.

14:04.398 --> 14:06.499
Whoo-wee, Chris! You're cute!

14:06.533 --> 14:08.167
Stewie, that's
Log Cabin.

14:08.202 --> 14:10.103
Uh, h-he gets the joke.

14:10.137 --> 14:12.105
I'm sorry, Chris.
Jerome just doesn't think

14:12.139 --> 14:14.107
his daughter should date
a white guy.

14:14.141 --> 14:16.109
Black racism
is the biggest problem

14:16.143 --> 14:17.944
facing this country today.

14:17.978 --> 14:20.480
You know, I should go
over there and fight for Pam.

14:20.514 --> 14:22.015
Absolutely you should.

14:22.049 --> 14:23.883
You should always fight
for what you believe in.

14:23.917 --> 14:25.451
Like Patrick Henry.

14:25.486 --> 14:28.421
Give me liberty
or give me death.

14:29.823 --> 14:31.457
Oh, that was easy.

14:31.492 --> 14:32.592
I know, right?

14:32.626 --> 14:34.694
Ryan wanted to give him liberty.

14:34.728 --> 14:37.063
You do the paperwork, Ryan.

14:40.301 --> 14:44.470
<i>And now the HBO
original series, Boys.</i>

14:44.505 --> 14:46.539
Hey, sorry I slept
with that girl you liked.

14:46.573 --> 14:47.674
Eh, it's cool.

14:47.708 --> 14:49.542
Did you walk around naked
after you had sex?

14:49.576 --> 14:51.878
What? No. No one
wants to see that.

14:51.912 --> 14:54.080
Isn't this time in our lives
so interesting?

14:54.114 --> 14:55.648
No.

14:55.683 --> 14:57.850
Griffin! Where the hell
is my daughter?

14:57.885 --> 15:00.953
She left me a note saying
she ran off with Chris.

15:00.988 --> 15:02.488
Oh, my God, Chris?

15:02.523 --> 15:04.991
That dirtbag hangs
around my daughter, too!

15:05.025 --> 15:06.526
I don't have time
for your nonsense.

15:06.560 --> 15:07.994
I got to find
my daughter.

15:08.028 --> 15:10.196
Look, let me help you!
I'm great at finding stuff.

15:10.230 --> 15:11.998
Last night, I found
Lois's G-spot.

15:12.032 --> 15:14.067
No, he didn't!
I didn't know she was home.

15:14.101 --> 15:16.336
I was able to please her
in other ways, though.

15:16.370 --> 15:18.771
No!
Okay, let's just go.

15:22.543 --> 15:24.010
My dad's such a jerk.

15:24.044 --> 15:26.946
I'm glad we ran away.
Yeah.

15:26.980 --> 15:30.750
So... what do people do
in motels?

15:30.784 --> 15:32.418
They get naked.

15:32.453 --> 15:35.555
Okay, but all I know about sex
is from Internet porn,

15:35.589 --> 15:38.658
so I'm very excited
to try buffering.

15:38.692 --> 15:40.793
Then I'll leave you alone

15:40.828 --> 15:42.895
to get undressed and
under the covers,

15:42.930 --> 15:44.897
and I'll be right back.

15:54.241 --> 15:56.809
Hey, I'm trying to sleep
and urinate here.

15:56.844 --> 15:58.611
Do you mind using
the other bed?

15:58.645 --> 15:59.679
Sorry.

15:59.713 --> 16:01.681
<i>I was the cousin in Vacation.</i>

16:01.715 --> 16:03.483
Yeah, I know who you are.

16:06.587 --> 16:08.221
How do I look?

16:08.255 --> 16:10.289
Oh, God. Are we at that part
of the relationship?

16:10.324 --> 16:11.691
You look fine!

16:11.725 --> 16:14.227
Pam, this may come
as a surprise to you,

16:14.261 --> 16:16.963
but I am not
an experienced lover.

16:16.997 --> 16:19.565
Don't worry. It's my
first time, too.

16:19.600 --> 16:22.368
Wow, I guess everybody
has a first time.

16:22.403 --> 16:24.670
<i>Even Maverick from Top Gun.</i>

16:24.705 --> 16:26.706
Thank you, pretty lady!

16:31.845 --> 16:35.214
So, all those other black
drivers that you're nodding at,

16:35.249 --> 16:36.816
do you know them?

16:42.723 --> 16:44.023
Ah, man.

16:44.057 --> 16:45.892
Look, relax. We'll just
tell him the truth.

16:45.926 --> 16:47.226
We're cruising
around town

16:47.261 --> 16:49.896
looking for a sexually active
14-year-old boy.

16:49.930 --> 16:52.632
You have any idea how
fast you were going?

16:52.666 --> 16:54.467
I was going the speed limit,
Officer.

16:54.501 --> 16:55.568
He was.

16:55.602 --> 16:57.103
Are you here against
your will, sir?

16:57.137 --> 16:59.772
If you're asking if I'd rather
be at the zoo, then yes.

16:59.807 --> 17:01.374
Maybe you step
out of the car

17:01.408 --> 17:03.409
and we see if you've
been drinking.

17:05.179 --> 17:09.449
I'm too fat to be
in the car by myself.

17:12.486 --> 17:15.588
The police pull me over for
made-up violations all the time.

17:15.622 --> 17:18.391
You don't know what it's like
to be treated like a criminal.

17:18.425 --> 17:20.059
What's it like?
Bad.

17:20.093 --> 17:21.627
Whoa.

17:21.662 --> 17:23.896
I've never broken a law
in my life, Peter.

17:23.931 --> 17:25.731
I'm a 42-year-old man,

17:25.766 --> 17:27.533
I own a business,
I pay my taxes,

17:27.568 --> 17:29.435
and yet I got to deal
with this crap

17:29.470 --> 17:31.137
every time
I step outside my house.

17:31.171 --> 17:35.107
Makes me so damn angry, I don't
know what to do with myself.

17:35.142 --> 17:36.509
Well, you should be like me.

17:36.543 --> 17:39.278
<i>Whenever I get angry,
I go do some Footloose dancing.</i>

18:03.770 --> 18:06.739
♪ You can never, never, never,
ever, never, never ♪

18:06.773 --> 18:10.376
♪ Never, ever hide your heart ♪

18:10.410 --> 18:12.612
♪ Don't ever, ever ♪

18:12.646 --> 18:17.717
♪ Ever, ever try ♪

18:17.751 --> 18:19.719
I'm also thinking
about ice creams.

18:19.753 --> 18:21.787
♪ Don't give... ♪

18:21.822 --> 18:23.923
Peter, you seem
like a nice guy.

18:23.957 --> 18:26.192
I don't mind having
you in my bar, man,

18:26.226 --> 18:28.494
but it's different when
it's your baby girl.

18:28.529 --> 18:31.097
I guess.
I just have boys.

18:31.131 --> 18:33.099
Forgive me for being
a protective father,

18:33.133 --> 18:35.835
but white people have exploited
and mistreated blacks

18:35.869 --> 18:39.805
for centuries, and I'm not gonna
let that happen to Pam.

18:39.840 --> 18:44.143
Wow, we've driven 55 miles
with the gas light on.

18:49.349 --> 18:51.450
Hold it right there!

18:51.485 --> 18:52.985
Dad! Jerome!

18:53.020 --> 18:54.620
How did you find us?!

18:54.655 --> 18:57.423
We didn't.
You just told us.

18:57.457 --> 18:58.491
You okay, honey?

18:58.525 --> 18:59.825
Dad, I'm fine.

18:59.860 --> 19:01.460
Don't worry.
Nothing happened.

19:01.495 --> 19:05.264
I tucked it between my legs
as a joke and then it got stuck.

19:05.299 --> 19:09.335
Look, I'm sorry, Chris, but we
got to respect Jerome's wishes.

19:09.369 --> 19:11.671
Now that I understand
what he's been through,

19:11.705 --> 19:13.940
I realize he's a good
man who has reason

19:13.974 --> 19:15.741
to be a little
suspicious of Whitey.

19:15.776 --> 19:17.743
Thank you
for understanding, Peter.

19:17.778 --> 19:20.212
Jerome is right. White is
white, black is black--

19:20.247 --> 19:22.214
got to keep the races
completely separate.

19:22.249 --> 19:25.151
That... wasn't
exactly my point.

19:25.185 --> 19:26.686
Chris, from now on,
I don't want you

19:26.720 --> 19:27.987
talking to any
black people.

19:28.021 --> 19:30.289
How the hell am I supposed
to get through airport security?

19:30.324 --> 19:31.624
We'll figure it out.

19:31.658 --> 19:33.292
It's the least we
can do for Jerome.

19:33.327 --> 19:35.161
Isn't that
right, Jerome?

19:39.666 --> 19:43.235
Is that the lesson
you want me to learn, Dad?

19:43.270 --> 19:45.438
No, baby.

19:45.472 --> 19:48.107
You know, Peter,
maybe I did overreact.

19:48.141 --> 19:50.176
Just 'cause I've experienced
some hard times

19:50.210 --> 19:53.512
doesn't mean this generation
can't teach us a thing or two.

19:53.547 --> 19:55.715
All right,

19:55.749 --> 19:57.617
if these kids want to date,

19:57.651 --> 19:59.830
then I guess
that's okay with me.

19:59.855 --> 20:03.855
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:03.991 --> 20:06.359
It takes a man with
a crazy big hog

20:06.393 --> 20:07.749
to admit when
he's wrong.

20:07.895 --> 20:10.597
Thanks, Peter.

20:13.291 --> 20:15.740
Hey, Jerome, you want to
help me kill Randy Quaid?

20:15.741 --> 20:16.872
Who?